codemap 9
tour feature-search-files
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The human, looking for text anywhere in the repo (a name a tour does not cover, a string, a pattern), without switching to an editor. Open the Search tab by clicking it, from the palette's 'search every file', or from back and forward: its regex field sits at the top of the view, above the hits, and takes the keyboard whenever the view is shown, so the next keystrokes are the pattern. Enter matches every line of every indexed file, up to 5000 hits (when there were more, the Search tab reads '5000+' and the view and the status bar say the list was cut), and lists them under a row per file, each with its line number and the line's text; the status bar gives the count. Clicking a hit opens its file in the Source view at that line; clicking a file row opens the file. A bad regex is refused in the status bar with the parser's last line. The field keeps its text, selected, so typing replaces it. When the view is hidden behind another tab of its panel, the field lets go of the keyboard, so keys reach the view in front. Where the field sits: in a run of the window before this layout, the field was at the left end of the top bar, labelled 'search', beside the back and forward arrows, while its hits opened in the centre Search tab, which read 'type a regex in the search box and press enter': the input sat a window-width from its output, and the arrows next to it read as a search history. The owner chose the field inside the Search view; the command palette (ctrl+p) is not a substitute, since it finds names (tours, steps, symbols, files, actions), not lines of text, and back and forward stay in the top bar, where they apply to every view.

